---
// Privacy policy (GDPR Art. 13). DRAFT: needs the controller's name/address and a legal check.
// RULE: whenever a service that touches visitor or subscriber data is added or removed,
// update this page AND the data map in the project's legal-compliance-checklist.md.
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
const updated = 'November 18, 2026';
---
<Base title="Privacy" description="How Gauge the Culture handles your data.">
  <article class="wrap legal">
    <p class="kicker">Privacy</p>
    <h1 class="hed legal__title">Privacy policy</h1>
    <p class="meta">Last updated {updated}</p>

    <div class="draft" role="note">
      <strong>Draft.</strong> This page is not final. The controller's name and address will be added after legal review.
    </div>

    <div class="prose legal__body">
      <h2>The short version</h2>
      <p>We collect as little as possible. No ads, no analytics, no tracking cookies. If you subscribe, we keep your email address. That's it.</p>

      <h2>Who is responsible</h2>
      <p>The controller under the GDPR is: <mark>[NAME]</mark>, <mark>[ADDRESS]</mark>. Contact: <a href="mailto:hello@gaugetheculture.com">hello@gaugetheculture.com</a>.</p>

      <h2>When you visit this site</h2>
      <p>Our host, Cloudflare, processes your IP address, browser details and the page you ask for. This is needed to deliver the site and protect it from attacks. Legal basis: our legitimate interest in a safe, working website (Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR). Our own server logs never contain email addresses, and we keep short-term logs only.</p>
      <p>Fonts are stored on our own server, so your browser does not contact Google or any other font service.</p>

      <h2>When you subscribe</h2>
      <p>We use your email address only to send you the newsletter. Legal basis: your consent (Art. 6(1)(a) GDPR).</p>
      <p>We use double opt-in. After you submit the form, we email you a confirmation link. You are subscribed only after you confirm.</p>
      <p>To stop bots, the form uses Cloudflare Turnstile. It checks signals such as your IP address, browser type and connection details. Legal basis: our legitimate interest in protecting the form (Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR). Cloudflare also uses this data to improve its bot detection, as its own controller. See the <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/turnstile-privacy-policy/" rel="noopener">Turnstile Privacy Addendum</a>.</p>
      <p>The newsletter is sent with Resend. Resend stores your email address and delivery information for us.</p>
      <p>You can withdraw your consent at any time. Use the unsubscribe link in any email, or write to us. We then stop sending and keep only a note that you unsubscribed, so we never email you again by mistake.</p>

      <h2>When you email us</h2>
      <p>Mail to hello@gaugetheculture.com is forwarded by Cloudflare Email Routing to our mailbox. We use your message only to reply. Legal basis: Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR.</p>

      <h2>Light and dark mode</h2>
      <p>If you use the light/dark switch, your browser saves that choice on your device. It is never sent to us. This is needed to give you the setting you asked for (§ 25(2) no. 2 TDDDG).</p>

      <h2>Service providers and transfers outside the EU</h2>
      <p>We use these providers, each under a data processing agreement (Art. 28 GDPR):</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Cloudflare, Inc.</strong> (USA): hosting, security, Turnstile, email forwarding.</li>
        <li><strong>Resend</strong> (USA): newsletter delivery and subscriber list.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Both are certified under the EU-U.S. Data Privacy Framework. Their agreements also include the EU Standard Contractual Clauses.</p>

      <h2>How long we keep data</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Email address: until you unsubscribe. After that, only a suppression note.</li>
        <li>Server logs: a few days.</li>
        <li>Emails you send us: as long as needed to handle your message.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Your rights</h2>
      <p>You have the right to access, correct, delete, restrict or export your data, and to object to processing based on legitimate interest (Art. 15–21 GDPR). You can withdraw consent at any time. Write to <a href="mailto:hello@gaugetheculture.com">hello@gaugetheculture.com</a>. We reply within one month.</p>
      <p>You can also complain to a data protection authority, for example the one where you live or where we are based.</p>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>When we add or remove a service, we update this page and the date at the top.</p>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .legal { padding-top: clamp(40px, 5vw, 72px); }
  .legal__title { font-size: clamp(48px, 6vw, 80px); margin: 16px 0 12px; }
  .legal__body { margin-inline: 0; }
  .legal__body h2 { font-size: clamp(26px, 2.4vw, 32px); margin-top: 48px; }
  .legal__body p, .legal__body li { font-size: 18px; }
  .legal__body ul { padding-left: 22px; margin: 16px 0 0; }
  .legal__body li { font-family: var(--read); line-height: 1.6; color: var(--tx); margin-top: 8px; }
  .legal__body mark { background: var(--sel); color: var(--tx); padding: 0 4px; }
  .draft {
    max-width: var(--measure); margin-top: 28px; padding: 14px 18px;
    border: 1px solid var(--acc); font-family: var(--sans); font-size: 14px; color: var(--tx2);
  }
</style>
